WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.150
Kaze ni kami ga nabiku

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.150
My hair flows in the wind.

00:00:05.150 --> 00:00:10.720
Kokoro ni hirogaru aozora no deai

00:00:05.150 --> 00:00:10.720
An encounter in the blue skies of our hearts...

00:00:11.290 --> 00:00:15.980
Tooku hanaretetemo

00:00:11.290 --> 00:00:15.980
Though we are apart,

00:00:15.980 --> 00:00:21.590
Kanjiru koto wa itsumo kimi dakara

00:00:15.980 --> 00:00:21.590
I'm always thinking about you,

00:00:21.590 --> 00:00:26.930
Itsu no hi ka mune wo hatte

00:00:21.590 --> 00:00:26.930
so let's promise to meet again

00:00:26.930 --> 00:00:32.410
Au koto wo yakusoku shiyou

00:00:26.930 --> 00:00:32.410
one day, with our heads held high.

00:00:32.410 --> 00:00:39.020
Zutto futari owari no nai

00:00:32.410 --> 00:00:39.020
We'll be together, like a dream

00:00:39.020 --> 00:00:45.410
Yume wo egaku you ni

00:00:39.020 --> 00:00:45.410
with no end.

00:00:45.410 --> 00:00:47.440
Kimi ni

00:00:45.410 --> 00:00:47.440
I want

00:00:47.440 --> 00:00:56.400
Kono omoi itsu no hi ka tsutaetai

00:00:47.440 --> 00:00:56.400
to tell you this someday.

00:00:58.180 --> 00:01:07.370
Sabishisa wo shiawase ni kaeru tame

00:00:58.180 --> 00:01:07.370
I'm right here next to you

00:01:09.140 --> 00:01:16.460
Soba ni iru yo kokoro wa

00:01:09.140 --> 00:01:16.460
to turn your loneliness into joy.

00:01:17.380 --> 00:01:24.830
Konna ni chikaku ni kanjiru

00:01:17.380 --> 00:01:24.830
I can feel your heart so close to mine.

00:01:31.630 --> 00:01:35.290
At the age of thirteen, Maya Kitajima faced many hardships,

00:01:35.290 --> 00:01:38.280
but was still drawn to the world of acting.

00:01:38.470 --> 00:01:43.550
Chigusa Tsukikage recognized Maya's natural talent in a flash.

00:01:43.660 --> 00:01:48.770
Maya was put forward to be cast in a play for her school's culture festival, but...

00:01:50.000 --> 00:01:54.950
Episode 3 - The Bird That Flew Away

00:01:55.470 --> 00:01:57.480
The king puts on a display of mercy:

00:01:57.480 --> 00:02:02.180
If this man condemned to death is taken by one of the maidens as her husband...

00:02:02.180 --> 00:02:02.740
Ouch!

00:02:02.740 --> 00:02:06.230
It's Vivi! Vivi the Fool has come.

00:02:06.610 --> 00:02:10.370
Huh? Are you calling me stupid?

00:02:11.610 --> 00:02:14.660
The Fool? The Fool? What does that mean, pray tell?

00:02:14.660 --> 00:02:18.060
Did you mean pool perchance?

00:02:18.520 --> 00:02:23.020
Did I fall in a pool? Is that it?

00:02:21.630 --> 00:02:23.020
Silence.

00:02:23.310 --> 00:02:25.240
The king puts on a display of mercy:

00:02:25.240 --> 00:02:30.310
If this man condemned to death is taken by one of the maidens as her husband,

00:02:30.310 --> 00:02:35.170
then she will redeem his sins and save his life.

00:02:38.380 --> 00:02:43.320
Um, if I meet the requirements, that means we can get married.

00:02:43.320 --> 00:02:48.050
But I'm unsightly and dimwitted and have no wedding gown to speak of.

00:02:48.050 --> 00:02:51.920
O vile criminal, the maiden attempting to marry you is...

00:02:51.920 --> 00:02:53.540
...the most simpleminded...

00:02:53.540 --> 00:02:55.630
...most hideous...

00:02:55.630 --> 00:02:58.040
...and the most ridiculed maiden in the land!

00:02:58.520 --> 00:03:04.980
What are you talking about?! I'd rather die than get married to a woman as pathetic as her!

00:03:06.500 --> 00:03:07.580
No doubt about it.

00:03:07.580 --> 00:03:08.300
No doubt about it.

00:03:08.300 --> 00:03:09.690
It'd be better to die.

00:03:18.050 --> 00:03:20.020
"Is that your daughter?"

00:03:20.280 --> 00:03:23.170
I'd be too ashamed to answer.

00:03:45.170 --> 00:03:49.090
It pains me so.

00:03:49.090 --> 00:03:55.010
It's not my fault that I'm so unsightly, dimwitted and pathetic.

00:04:02.110 --> 00:04:04.170
What are you doing, Kitajima?!

00:04:04.170 --> 00:04:08.700
Make them laugh! Follow the script and make them laugh!

00:04:10.090 --> 00:04:14.180
So you're telling me you'd rather die than marry me?

00:04:14.180 --> 00:04:18.380
Oh God, stick to your lines! The lines!

00:04:18.900 --> 00:04:23.180
Is marrying me really worse than death?

00:04:23.170 --> 00:04:24.450
Y-Yes!

00:04:25.300 --> 00:04:29.330
Ah, I knew what was in store for me and yet still, I persevered.

00:04:39.270 --> 00:04:42.030
What's everyone doing?!

00:04:42.030 --> 00:04:44.970
You're supposed to be laughing and scorning her!

00:04:44.970 --> 00:04:46.440
Laugh!

00:04:50.630 --> 00:04:55.640
Ever since I was born, I've been a laughingstock and I've grown accustomed to it.

00:04:56.400 --> 00:05:00.510
Yet I've never felt as low as this.

00:05:01.720 --> 00:05:04.350
I want to die.

00:05:04.860 --> 00:05:09.330
For what have I been living up to this point?

00:05:10.060 --> 00:05:12.200
Oh God, it's turned into a train wreck.

00:05:12.200 --> 00:05:14.590
The audience look subdued...

00:05:14.590 --> 00:05:16.730
Curtain! Lower the curtain!

00:05:32.470 --> 00:05:34.060
That was magnificent!

00:05:34.060 --> 00:05:34.810
Bravo!

00:05:34.810 --> 00:05:35.490
You've gotta be kidding!

00:05:35.490 --> 00:05:36.190
Amazing!

00:05:36.190 --> 00:05:37.720
Yeah!

00:05:45.070 --> 00:05:46.080
Ma'am.

00:05:46.400 --> 00:05:47.670
Genzo...

00:05:47.670 --> 00:05:49.360
Please hang in there.

00:05:58.080 --> 00:05:59.570
Maya,

00:06:00.620 --> 00:06:02.080
that was amazing.

00:06:02.080 --> 00:06:06.500
Looks like I lost the lead, but that was really something.

00:06:08.710 --> 00:06:10.620
I was so surprised, Maya.

00:06:11.100 --> 00:06:14.790
I didn't realize how sad Vivi actually was.

00:06:16.120 --> 00:06:17.370
Kitajima!

00:06:17.370 --> 00:06:22.420
Don't get any ideas! The stage isn't your sole property.

00:06:22.960 --> 00:06:24.180
Yes...

00:06:27.210 --> 00:06:29.080
Oh, Ms. Kitajima.

00:06:29.080 --> 00:06:32.110
You didn't come and watch Maya's play?

00:06:32.110 --> 00:06:35.750
Well... I had something I had to...

00:06:36.050 --> 00:06:39.250
Everyone was applauding and cheering for Maya.

00:06:40.800 --> 00:06:44.190
I was taken aback by how good she was.

00:06:44.190 --> 00:06:48.520
B-But she had the most pathetic role...

00:06:48.520 --> 00:06:52.060
What are you talking about? The audience loved her!

00:06:52.060 --> 00:06:55.680
If you'd been there, you would have been so proud.

00:06:56.710 --> 00:06:57.790
Maya...

00:06:57.790 --> 00:06:59.060
That girl...

00:07:02.420 --> 00:07:03.660
Delivery.

00:07:04.290 --> 00:07:06.090
Thank you very much.

00:07:18.370 --> 00:07:20.330
Ondine

00:07:18.370 --> 00:07:20.330
Looking for Research Students

00:07:21.520 --> 00:07:23.160
Ondine...

00:07:25.590 --> 00:07:30.500
I want to perform in another play...

00:07:47.000 --> 00:07:50.830
Theatrical Troupe Ondine

00:07:47.000 --> 00:07:50.830
Beware of the Dog

00:07:47.980 --> 00:07:51.270
Excuse me, I saw your ad...

00:07:51.270 --> 00:07:54.930
I see. One moment please.

00:07:54.930 --> 00:07:56.870
This is the application form.

00:07:56.870 --> 00:08:01.720
Place a photo here, list all your previous roles and submit it.

00:08:01.720 --> 00:08:04.170
Then, there'll be a series of admission exams.

00:08:04.860 --> 00:08:07.330
A-Admission exams?

00:08:07.970 --> 00:08:12.940
Written, acting, singing, pantomime and dance. Not to mention the interview...

00:08:12.940 --> 00:08:15.000
We'll notify you if you pass.

00:08:15.000 --> 00:08:17.720
You will also need to pay the admissions fee and the monthly fees.

00:08:18.520 --> 00:08:19.780
Excuse me.

00:08:19.780 --> 00:08:22.240
You forgot your application form.

00:08:22.430 --> 00:08:24.180
My word...

00:08:25.260 --> 00:08:31.110
I don't need it. We just don't have that kind of money.

00:08:31.110 --> 00:08:32.630
You there, repeat it again.

00:08:34.190 --> 00:08:37.250
"You realize that I know your secret, don't you?"

00:08:37.250 --> 00:08:39.500
No, your eyes aren't laughing.

00:08:42.780 --> 00:08:44.200
How often must I repeat myself?

00:08:44.200 --> 00:08:48.540
Your mouth is laughing but your eyes and the rest of your body isn't!

00:08:48.540 --> 00:08:52.110
You need to laugh with more scorn, as though you've already claimed victory.

00:08:52.110 --> 00:08:53.510
What's with that girl?

00:08:52.980 --> 00:08:58.010
Listen, you have him cornered. Look down on him. Use your whole body.

00:08:53.510 --> 00:08:56.540
She's freaking me out, staring at us.

00:08:56.540 --> 00:08:58.790
She's just a kid. Ignore her.

00:08:58.790 --> 00:08:59.810
You got that?

00:08:59.810 --> 00:09:00.470
Yes.

00:09:00.470 --> 00:09:02.480
Then, let's do it again.

00:09:03.440 --> 00:09:06.480
"You realize that I know your secret, don't you?"

00:09:06.480 --> 00:09:09.550
Step forward. Be confident and corner him!

00:09:17.680 --> 00:09:19.430
One, two, three, four,

00:09:19.430 --> 00:09:21.100
and five, six, seven.

00:09:21.100 --> 00:09:23.390
And two, three, four,

00:09:23.390 --> 00:09:25.940
and five, six, seven, eight.

00:09:25.940 --> 00:09:27.820
Okay, let's take a break.

00:09:27.820 --> 00:09:30.260
She's still watching us.

00:09:30.260 --> 00:09:32.400
She's been there for two hours.

00:09:42.040 --> 00:09:43.040
Oh dear!

00:09:43.560 --> 00:09:45.330
Sakurakouji?

00:09:49.680 --> 00:09:51.760
Good boy.

00:09:56.350 --> 00:09:57.460
Are you all right?

00:09:57.690 --> 00:09:59.220
Yes...

00:09:59.780 --> 00:10:01.140
Where's the Nurse's Office?

00:10:01.140 --> 00:10:03.010
Call a doctor!

00:10:19.890 --> 00:10:22.270
Well, I'm glad it's nothing serious.

00:10:22.270 --> 00:10:24.170
I'm fine. Thank you.

00:10:24.780 --> 00:10:28.520
What were you doing today, sitting in a place like that?

00:10:28.520 --> 00:10:32.780
I was thinking it would be great to be in a troupe like that one.

00:10:33.780 --> 00:10:37.840
But it's really expensive, so there's no way I could join.

00:10:38.270 --> 00:10:40.270
Hey, are you okay?

00:10:40.550 --> 00:10:42.460
If you'd told the receptionist or one of the students,

00:10:42.460 --> 00:10:44.180
the dog wouldn't have barked at you.

00:10:44.510 --> 00:10:47.210
Thank you for saving me.

00:10:47.210 --> 00:10:51.320
I heard you were hanging from that windowsill for two hours.

00:10:51.930 --> 00:10:53.360
Two hours?

00:10:53.600 --> 00:10:57.510
When I was watching the rehearsal, I became absorbed...

00:10:59.000 --> 00:11:00.470
Maya Kitajima...

00:11:00.470 --> 00:11:02.250
Hey, Masumi,

00:11:02.460 --> 00:11:04.180
sorry for making you wait. Shall we get going?

00:11:04.730 --> 00:11:07.130
Oh, you're...

00:11:10.350 --> 00:11:12.930
That girl wants to join?

00:11:12.930 --> 00:11:16.630
Apparently she knows the son of Daito Troupe's President as well.

00:11:16.630 --> 00:11:18.820
How on earth does she know Mr. Hayami?!

00:11:18.820 --> 00:11:21.230
It looks like she knows Director Onodera as well.

00:11:21.230 --> 00:11:23.590
Who is this girl?

00:11:24.180 --> 00:11:27.840
Listen up, everyone. This girl wants to watch us for a bit. Her name's...

00:11:27.840 --> 00:11:29.500
Maya Kitajima.

00:11:30.690 --> 00:11:33.180
So, which troupe were you in before this one?

00:11:33.180 --> 00:11:35.480
Um, none.

00:11:35.480 --> 00:11:38.140
Are you in your school's Drama Club or something?

00:11:38.140 --> 00:11:39.930
No, I'm not.

00:11:39.930 --> 00:11:41.800
Seriously?

00:11:41.800 --> 00:11:44.170
Then, what acting experience do you have?

00:11:44.780 --> 00:11:50.020
Just one play, for the anniversary of my school's founding.

00:11:50.020 --> 00:11:52.880
Ha! Just one play! And a school play at that!

00:11:52.880 --> 00:11:54.160
A complete novice!

00:11:55.620 --> 00:11:57.850
Why are you laughing so hard?

00:11:57.850 --> 00:12:00.020
We're all novices until we make our debut.

00:12:00.020 --> 00:12:04.710
For your information, this school is the cream of the crop...

00:12:04.710 --> 00:12:06.770
and has molded a number of famous superstars.

00:12:06.770 --> 00:12:09.000
You're just...

00:12:11.480 --> 00:12:15.850
Sorry I'm late. The scene for the movie took longer than we expected.

00:12:17.110 --> 00:12:18.940
It's Ayumi Himekawa.

00:12:19.350 --> 00:12:23.150
She's the daughter of Utako Himekawa, the woman who stars in <i>La Dame aux Camelias</i>.

00:12:26.760 --> 00:12:31.280
Okay, let's begin today's pantomime rehearsal.

00:12:31.280 --> 00:12:33.580
Today's topic is "The Bird That Flew Away."

00:12:33.580 --> 00:12:35.790
Everyone will go in order.

00:12:36.040 --> 00:12:41.140
Sir, please, can this girl go first? She wants to join our troupe.

00:12:41.140 --> 00:12:42.560
What? But...

00:12:42.560 --> 00:12:46.020
Apparently, she came here wanting to join. So...

00:12:46.020 --> 00:12:49.440
But I haven't done pantomime before.

00:12:49.440 --> 00:12:51.840
You do want to join, don't you?

00:12:51.840 --> 00:12:54.950
It'd just be strange if you couldn't do it.

00:12:54.950 --> 00:12:57.620
Leave her alone! Can't you see she's in distress?

00:12:57.620 --> 00:13:02.920
Hm... why not approach it as if it were a test.

00:13:04.310 --> 00:13:05.730
But...

00:13:08.230 --> 00:13:12.990
We heard you weren't feeling well, so we've come to wish you a speedy recovery.

00:13:12.990 --> 00:13:18.760
Thank you, but I've already recovered, Mister Masumi, Mister Onodera.

00:13:18.760 --> 00:13:21.440
That's great news!

00:13:21.820 --> 00:13:23.100
It is?

00:13:23.100 --> 00:13:27.240
I would have thought it would suit you better if I died sooner rather than later.

00:13:27.240 --> 00:13:29.310
Nonsense!

00:13:29.310 --> 00:13:31.020
Don't lie.

00:13:31.020 --> 00:13:37.430
If I die, you finally get your hands on the performing rights to <i>The Scarlet Angel</i>.

00:13:38.130 --> 00:13:42.550
I admit that we desire those rights so that we can stage <i>The Scarlet Angel</i>.

00:13:42.550 --> 00:13:49.980
Thirty-two years ago, the <i>The Scarlet Angel</i> was written by inspired playwright, Ichiren Ozaki,

00:13:49.980 --> 00:13:54.180
and you starred in the lead role, eliciting a performance that struck a chord with everyone who saw it.

00:13:55.960 --> 00:14:02.730
After its debut, <i>The Scarlet Angel</i> became a runaway hit, being performed more than three-hundred times.

00:14:03.070 --> 00:14:12.780
However, the author, Ichiren Ozaki, then announced that only Chigusa Tsukikage was capable...

00:14:12.780 --> 00:14:17.320
of being the Scarlet Angel and denied the role to even the most famous actresses;

00:14:17.960 --> 00:14:25.390
in the same way that Junji Kinoshita only allowed Yasue Yamamoto to perform as Otsuu,

00:14:25.390 --> 00:14:28.510
the lead role in <i>The Twilight Crane</i>.

00:14:30.450 --> 00:14:39.290
On his deathbed, Ichiren Ozaki gave you sole rights to <i>The Scarlet Angel</i>.

00:14:39.290 --> 00:14:42.370
You continued to perform the play...

00:14:48.480 --> 00:14:49.740
That's true.

00:14:50.160 --> 00:14:56.050
But a stage light fell from the rafters and disfigured my face beyond repair.

00:14:56.050 --> 00:14:59.350
My acting career was snuffed out in that instant.

00:15:00.290 --> 00:15:03.460
Since then, you haven't once set foot on stage.

00:15:03.460 --> 00:15:10.390
And before granting anyone else the rights to <i>The Scarlet Angel</i>, one day you disappeared.

00:15:13.510 --> 00:15:20.600
Since then, <i>The Scarlet Angel</i> has become the ghost of a masterpiece that no one could perform,

00:15:20.600 --> 00:15:23.870
and it's been sealed away like that for twenty years.

00:15:26.070 --> 00:15:31.470
And then, you finally appear again, here in Tokyo.

00:15:31.470 --> 00:15:38.390
It has been a lifelong dream of my venerable father, the founder of the Daito Corporation, to stage <i>The Scarlet Angel</i>,

00:15:38.390 --> 00:15:40.850
as well as my own.

00:15:40.850 --> 00:15:45.350
It would be directed by none other than Japan's finest: Mister Onodera.

00:15:45.350 --> 00:15:47.270
Utako Himekawa would take the lead role.

00:15:47.270 --> 00:15:49.430
Utako Himekawa?

00:15:50.680 --> 00:15:54.230
Utako Himekawa used to be your very own apprentice.

00:15:55.560 --> 00:15:58.380
I can't imagine that you'd object to this choice of actress.

00:15:58.620 --> 00:16:00.390
What do you say, Ms. Tsukikage?

00:16:00.390 --> 00:16:04.800
Won't you consider granting us permission to stage <i>The Scarlet Angel</i>?

00:16:05.120 --> 00:16:09.610
Of course, we'll pay the appropriate licensing fees.

00:16:11.410 --> 00:16:13.400
Can you wait another ten years?

00:16:13.910 --> 00:16:15.280
Ten years?

00:16:15.280 --> 00:16:18.980
Unfortunately, none of today's actresses, including Utako Himekawa,

00:16:18.980 --> 00:16:22.740
are capable of playing the Scarlet Angel.

00:16:22.740 --> 00:16:24.090
But ma'am...

00:16:24.350 --> 00:16:29.150
That's why I've been secretly planning to open an acting school...

00:16:29.150 --> 00:16:34.340
aimed specifically at training an actress who'll be able to star as the Scarlet Angel.

00:16:34.950 --> 00:16:37.300
And I've finally found her!

00:16:38.590 --> 00:16:40.490
The actress who can play her!

00:16:40.490 --> 00:16:41.730
Who is it?

00:16:41.730 --> 00:16:44.670
Which actress could possibly top Utako Himekawa?!

00:16:44.940 --> 00:16:46.680
You'll find out soon enough.

00:16:46.680 --> 00:16:47.760
Soon enough.

00:16:59.900 --> 00:17:02.660
Tea is served.

00:17:03.180 --> 00:17:05.220
Okay, are you ready?

00:17:05.220 --> 00:17:08.300
Yes. I'll do it. Please let me try.

00:17:13.600 --> 00:17:15.000
A bird that flew away.

00:17:15.210 --> 00:17:16.710
A bird that flew away.

00:17:16.710 --> 00:17:18.860
Express it using only my body.

00:17:18.860 --> 00:17:20.840
Only using my body.

00:17:24.960 --> 00:17:27.670
This is my room.

00:17:27.670 --> 00:17:29.380
This is inside my room.

00:17:36.560 --> 00:17:40.010
There's a bird cage in my room.

00:17:40.400 --> 00:17:46.280
The bird that takes flight in the room when I try to feed it.

00:18:02.640 --> 00:18:04.820
What's this?! I can see it...

00:18:17.870 --> 00:18:21.050
She's just standing there like an idiot.

00:18:21.050 --> 00:18:22.500
She looks like a statue.

00:18:22.500 --> 00:18:24.610
A statue?

00:18:24.610 --> 00:18:26.510
Look at her eyes.

00:18:26.510 --> 00:18:29.530
She can't even see us right now.

00:18:29.530 --> 00:18:33.200
That's because she's in a completely different room, chasing a bird.

00:18:33.200 --> 00:18:34.680
See? It's on top of the dresser.

00:18:34.680 --> 00:18:37.860
It flew off... It's flying around now.

00:18:38.040 --> 00:18:42.640
Just by looking at her eyes, you can see all of the bird's movements.

00:18:42.640 --> 00:18:46.040
But you can't catch a bird by just standing there.

00:18:46.040 --> 00:18:49.270
Yeah, the topic mentioned catching it too.

00:19:00.400 --> 00:19:01.950
What's she doing?

00:19:01.950 --> 00:19:03.470
She's just standing there.

00:19:03.470 --> 00:19:04.960
Catch it already!

00:19:04.960 --> 00:19:11.150
But it's too high up and I don't know how to catch it.

00:19:11.150 --> 00:19:12.660
What?!

00:19:12.660 --> 00:19:15.380
The bird's landed somewhere out of reach?

00:19:15.380 --> 00:19:16.950
Did she really go that far?

00:20:12.750 --> 00:20:15.990
Amazing... so this is what real acting is.

00:20:15.990 --> 00:20:19.490
She must be a true genius.

00:20:21.750 --> 00:20:29.040
That's ridiculous. She just said she didn't know how to catch the bird because it was too high up.

00:20:29.040 --> 00:20:31.300
What a stupid kid.

00:20:31.300 --> 00:20:33.550
You're the stupid ones.

00:20:33.740 --> 00:20:37.600
The fact she was troubled by it means that her acting has transcended mere acting...

00:20:37.600 --> 00:20:39.990
and has become real.

00:20:39.990 --> 00:20:44.600
That meant she refused to make any compromises even though the pantomime task required it.

00:20:45.260 --> 00:20:49.680
She visualized the bird landing somewhere high up.

00:20:50.150 --> 00:20:51.930
I could see it as well.

00:20:51.930 --> 00:20:54.670
The movement of her eyes showed me everything the bird was doing.

00:20:54.670 --> 00:20:57.720
That's why I could pick up where she left off so easily.

00:20:58.050 --> 00:21:01.150
It's true that her acting abilities are childish at best,

00:21:01.150 --> 00:21:03.150
but she put her whole body into her first attempt at pantomime...

00:21:03.150 --> 00:21:06.020
and toughed it out until the very end.

00:21:06.020 --> 00:21:09.940
Her courage alone puts her out of your league.

00:21:09.940 --> 00:21:13.780
You should be grateful she didn't make it into our troupe.

00:21:13.780 --> 00:21:18.920
If she ever does, all of you will be reduced to supporting roles.

00:21:23.390 --> 00:21:30.260
The shock of seeing Ayumi Himekawa's vivid acting had put Maya Kitajima into a gloomy mood.

00:21:31.000 --> 00:21:37.320
At the same age, Ayumi is considered a prodigy. Will she ever be able...

00:21:37.320 --> 00:21:41.300
to grow enough to be able to stand alongside Ayumi?

00:21:41.740 --> 00:21:48.890
Maya realized that she was stepping into a daunting, unknown world.

00:21:58.020 --> 00:22:03.930
Gomennette iwaretara

00:21:58.020 --> 00:22:03.930
When you say "I'm sorry,"

00:22:04.980 --> 00:22:10.670
Anata wo semerarenai yo

00:22:04.980 --> 00:22:10.670
I can't blame you.

00:22:11.950 --> 00:22:21.510
Sonna watashi wo kitto shitterundeshou

00:22:11.950 --> 00:22:21.510
I'm sure you know that's how I am.

00:22:21.510 --> 00:22:25.810
Nee zurui yo

00:22:21.510 --> 00:22:25.810
That's not fair.

00:22:26.510 --> 00:22:33.620
Yasashisa ni damasaretatte

00:22:26.510 --> 00:22:33.620
Even if I'm being fooled by kindness,

00:22:33.620 --> 00:22:44.210
Anata nara isso iito shinjita

00:22:33.620 --> 00:22:44.210
I believed that with you, it might be worth it.

00:22:44.210 --> 00:22:53.690
Sayonara wa doushite itoshiindarou

00:22:44.210 --> 00:22:53.690
Why are goodbyes so precious,

00:22:53.690 --> 00:22:58.250
Hanareteyuku noni

00:22:53.690 --> 00:22:58.250
even though they mean we're separating?

00:22:58.250 --> 00:23:07.640
Ushinatta ondo wo oboeteruyo

00:22:58.250 --> 00:23:07.640
I remember how it got colder.

00:23:07.640 --> 00:23:13.500
Yurushitai dakara anata

00:23:07.640 --> 00:23:13.500
I want to forgive you, so please don't go.

00:23:13.500 --> 00:23:21.410
Ikanaide douka ikanaide

00:23:13.500 --> 00:23:21.410
Whatever you do... just don't go.

00:23:24.260 --> 00:23:29.780
My mother, Utako Himekawa, is an actress who is said to be capable of playing the role of the Scarlet Angel.

00:23:31.030 --> 00:23:37.080
But Ms. Tsukikage seems to have her heart set on training an actress to play the Scarlet Angel herself.

00:23:37.470 --> 00:23:40.530
Is the girl whose miming conjured a bird capable...

00:23:40.530 --> 00:23:44.740
of surpassing my mother and meeting Ms. Tsukikage's expectations?

00:23:45.270 --> 00:23:49.280
I know I will surpass my mother.

00:23:47.000 --> 00:23:51.500
Episode 4 - The Stairs of Fire
